oices ["q-20963/selection/23e6dcfb2ec92058b5b0df132b0a847c744e92e7799d080003202700020cce9b" "q-20963/selection/b281b0c65b28852a265e45d86efbe0f872541b03035b263e65e84f5f30e8f7a0" "q-20963/selection/cbdeded4c006090099ae86a6e1e41610127880cabb93b28cf02701db27cf2b00" "q-20963/selection/06ae84c80d8b7a85f13dd1c6540ac1595327d33cff93efa97642d58e0a0488d4" "q-20963/selection/a16d9749ca0fb6cc7b7f63894f4252b36de77f0012e6df2eef95995aef36edba"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-20963" :question/id #uuid "f0787607-5bca-5e97-b7f4-40db59c2425f" :question/math-academy-id "q-20963" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 8 & 16 & -8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 8 & 16 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-8){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y=-1 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+2y=-1.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=-1-2y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1-2y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1-2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-20963/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97cd9132-458b-5234-a3d2-22b633acb74c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-20963"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73738/selection/1cb23fed8432f4b47c598ebe40e34a5dd63112b602530ef38eb50f5897eafe56" :answer/id #uuid "2c195dd0-eb81-5875-976a-a093838b8853" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-2-3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73738/selection/f3d3db9cb4a090852d77da52c42bcc6e2d881fc2d0485858f50d3e4f03c2fc10" :answer/id #uuid "36d84cc3-78f8-5a9d-ae00-dd3d24948008" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2+3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73738/selection/1179f41f3dd7a7b100b89c9b9efda4372f36799c5f6477d476b2328138ae1bf2" :answer/id #uuid "831e7e0a-aed0-5ddf-b0ff-b8a7a383aa33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-2,\\,-3⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73738/selection/eee4c512f52893eea9300bdb23bf00f606e843cd3d30bbc8087db4c3b2d034a9" :answer/id #uuid "9853f3f2-3c76-59b2-a379-62cf6f71ab60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-2,\\,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73738/selection/8e78b4b579b8ba86f8d45a316837c190897acaf2bfc817533536af48ea13d70c" :answer/id #uuid "6626a63d-9e1d-5478-a4a4-2f51d2d4d493" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-2+3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73738/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "60f91179-c02c-52de-821c-db603b09c9de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73738/selection/8e78b4b579b8ba86f8d45a316837c190897acaf2bfc817533536af48ea13d70c" :answer-field/choices ["q-73738/selection/1cb23fed8432f4b47c598ebe40e34a5dd63112b602530ef38eb50f5897eafe56" "q-73738/selection/f3d3db9cb4a090852d77da52c42bcc6e2d881fc2d0485858f50d3e4f03c2fc10" "q-73738/selection/1179f41f3dd7a7b100b89c9b9efda4372f36799c5f6477d476b2328138ae1bf2" "q-73738/selection/eee4c512f52893eea9300bdb23bf00f606e843cd3d30bbc8087db4c3b2d034a9" "q-73738/selection/8e78b4b579b8ba86f8d45a316837c190897acaf2bfc817533536af48ea13d70c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73738" :question/id #uuid "d0a05944-cd54-5fbe-bad9-a47ce86875e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-73738" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-3y=-2 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-3y=-2.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=-2+3y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-2+3y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=⟨-2+3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-73738/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97cd9132-458b-5234-a3d2-22b633acb74c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73738"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73740/selection/985f6b5ef1c8517ebf2244547e58da77a03c4a2e843c87009b203c6ea3c30ce0" :answer/id #uuid "f19c4b5d-373e-56d0-a2d5-a2f69be406d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begi