006090099ae86a6e1e41610127880cabb93b28cf02701db27cf2b00" "q-73740/selection/97eb79679ccb3934932b3ccf7a0c5d85f5a0b43df917664443be38411d32857a" "q-73740/selection/c16f73c6dcd2feff45d079ef404d7c8b47cf8f04221ee0cbcf38ede15c995ec9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73740" :question/id #uuid "28d32302-16b0-5cdc-a69e-754fd94318a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-73740" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -10 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -10 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y=-1 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+2y=-1.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=-1-2y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1-2y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1-2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73740/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97cd9132-458b-5234-a3d2-22b633acb74c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73740"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73750/selection/0807287fd3e8239f1ed27932089a620d7fcab85eab35e816c3d4a768986777d3" :answer/id #uuid "cbfd7428-1d1d-5ad8-8054-e1349712bb03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4+2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73750/selection/53ed3e016aba21b6407f9fed8eef7fdc6271a9904e7f496fbc5c08c4d39b2be3" :answer/id #uuid "f915a012-6351-5d0d-ba7a-0b98a70a6a96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4-2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73750/selection/6d6811ceb4fb69a54ce1b24e6804e5f0148bafa1b76b847b06436eb966d36b67" :answer/id #uuid "f95f3d05-0823-54d3-9f52-27fd855eef25" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No solution" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73750/selection/6f56db1fdad44b849d5aef3d2fd1d6e98016695476b51c7b7270920b420d1337" :answer/id #uuid "2e2e79a8-0e70-5741-b9be-f622b3aa6697" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2+4y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73750/selection/a16d9749ca0fb6cc7b7f63894f4252b36de77f0012e6df2eef95995aef36edba" :answer/id #uuid "ec2da10a-189d-5939-bcce-517cbd6aec24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-4y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73750/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "834515f8-6272-5827-bfac-7bf41c342fd2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73750/selection/0807287fd3e8239f1ed27932089a620d7fcab85eab35e816c3d4a768986777d3" :answer-field/choices ["q-73750/selection/0807287fd3e8239f1ed27932089a620d7fcab85eab35e816c3d4a768986777d3" "q-73750/selection/53ed3e016aba21b6407f9fed8eef7fdc6271a9904e7f496fbc5c08c4d39b2be3" "q-73750/selection/6d6811ceb4fb69a54ce1b24e6804e5f0148bafa1b76b847b06436eb966d36b67" "q-73750/selection/6f56db1fdad44b849d5aef3d2fd1d6e98016695476b51c7b7270920b420d1337" "q-73750/selection/a16d9749ca0fb6cc7b7f63894f4252b36de77f0012e6df2eef95995aef36edba"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73750" :question/id #uuid "79d64547-fc54-5cd3-a6ec-b00c0e085729" :question/math-academy-id "q-73750" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y=4 \\\\ -3x+6y=-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 6 & -12\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 6 & -12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y=4 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-2y=4.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=4+2y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=4+2y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4+2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-73750/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07f2ae4c-ff07-5b99-a7b0-90f460081eef"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73750"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-20960/selection/7437c2bee085b4fd3dc30f18a12ed6ee4423d10cce82628e15937e1fa5c2de67" :answer/id #uuid "4c556f67-0753-5b7c-a38e-c94576a87078" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-5-3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20960/selection/9e229afd731dc3186625b18eb3982e5bcde6a97923b6311a204b46010bbfaa97" :answer/id #uuid "1224a1fa-95e5-59ba-982b-b310df917b85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-5-4y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20960/selection/fbe85ee816846719bba3803aa913fdf2429601b6838fb3b0ee2166fd08de6fa9" :answer/id #uuid "ace1319c-d083-5c05-b8f5-32fb3d96eefa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5-3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20960/selection/f98f461fcc13230dd0665b55e3557023c0a55267e7b0124d8cb8f1997320f9a1" :answer/id #uuid "3ed7fdf0-ad1a-5e90-ad15-5c8cd647ae35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5-4y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20960/selection/6d6811ceb4fb69a54ce1b24e6804e5f0148bafa1b76b847b06436eb966d36b67" :answer/id #uuid "88ea9fc0-fe8a-5659-adca-ffc88484a23f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No solution" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20960/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c6ec63e8-3c68-578a-b514-6bbe727e8dd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-20960/selection/9e229afd731dc3186625b18eb3982e5bcde6a97923b6311a204b46010bbfaa97" :answer-field/choices ["q-20960/selection/7437c2bee085b4fd3dc30f18a12ed6ee4423d10cce82628e15937e1fa5c2de67" "q-20960/selection/9e229afd731dc3186625b18eb3982e5bcde6a97923b6311a204b46010bbfaa97" "q-20960/selection/fbe85ee816846719bba3803aa913fdf2429601b6838fb3b0ee2166fd08de6fa9" "q-20960/selection/f98f461fcc13230dd0665b55e3557023c0a55267e7b0124d8cb8f1997320f9a1" "q-20960/selection/6d6811ceb4fb69a54ce1b24e6804e5f0148bafa1b76b847b06436eb966d36b67"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-20960" :question/id #uuid "1aae5f9f-6428-5d27-b8a2-86cf26a0a204" :question/math-academy-id "q-20960" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}8x+32y=-40 \\\\ 5x+20y=-25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 32 & -40 \\\\ 5 & 20 & -25\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}8 & 32 & -40 \\\\ 5 & 20 & -25\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 20 & -25\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+4y=-5 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+4y=-5.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=-5-4y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-5-4y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-5-4y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-20960/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07f2ae4c-ff07-5b99-a7b0-90f460081eef"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-20960"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4699"] :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/assets/bd19fd1559a516610f03446ba40c8e0d620575f1ea8b736e9ed4ce07b099253c.png)\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/assets/49ca24beba2af93482e8e08a7edd396a2714b17f84decd26199741c728ab1bfa.png)\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y = 0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx - 3y = 1.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=1+3y,$ and the general solution is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/assets/71e9e1302c0aea79de3370541f0c25acb679e37a5527c172c9490693a4f74c30.png)\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=⟨1+3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4700"] :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/assets/13df05563b5770bd877481f24da1c69874d73594e6b82230a2159f01367ba030.png)\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/assets/4aff0484efeeb7e39af2bdb169b6fff07ce8ba9348ff3a4839423bf5c9ead97d.png)\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 10 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{5}{2} & 2 \\\\ 4 & 10 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{5}{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/assets/8a7e8b15bc463b00d805547aa64079a1474b5a4595555a5664fba7bfdfb7f62c.png)\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=-8$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=-8,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution." :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
